[[16,96,16384,"<h3>Functional description</h3><p>When the ignition key for the switch \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>H1</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is\nturned to the extreme position (AVV) [START], the solenoid winding\n(pin 50) of the starter motor \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>A20</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is supplied.</p><p>This supply comes from the battery via the\nline of maxifuse IGN of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B99</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>This supply is only present if there is\na safety signal - gear lever on P or N - coming from the unit on\nthe gearbox \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>L50</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              : this signal energizes the starting enablement\nrelay \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>J05</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , so that it sends the supply to pin 50 of the starter\nmotor \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>A20</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>Pin 30 of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>A20</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , the actual starter\nmotor, receives the voltage coming directly from the battery \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>A1</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>The direct current generated by the alternator \n\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>A10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               (pin B+) is sent to the battery \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>A1</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               through motor \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>A20</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .\nWhen the alternator is not turning and therefore not recharging\nthe battery, an earth signal is sent from pin D+ to check module \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E30,\npin 7.</strong></p><p>Module \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E30 receives a supply controlled\nby the ignition (INT) at pin 13 from the line protected by fuse\nF4 of the additional fuse box B98B: when this signal arrives, the\n&#x27;recharging&#x27; warning light comes on.</strong></p><p>When the engine has been started up this\nsignal becomes 12 V and the warning light goes out.</p>"]]